{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/129428-spoof-and-paradox","id":129428,"title":"spoof and paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-09T17:35:49-07:00","id":129428,"title":"spoof and paradox","content":"If demon I is the lone one witnessing a mage do magic since no risk of paradox reveals that the demon isn't human can a demon chose to spoof this event? <br /> <br /> my vote is yes because not doing so reveals you as not human but it is an iffy yes and I would appreciate others opinions on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:24:10-07:00","id":129466,"title":"","content":"I could be mistaken, but if the demon can observe said mage casting magic, wouldn't the magic be considered vulgar? As such, I would think there would still be a paradox risk regardless of the presence of witnesses (I'm a little rusty on my Mage rules so someone correct me if I'm wrong, it would just be a lesser risk for paradox than casting in front of a sleeper?) As such, I'm not sure the lack of paradox is adequate to reveal the demon's not-human nature. Even if it does come down to witnessing the casting, Sleepwalkers aren't likely to cause a paradox when witnessing magic and are considered human, right? So it's not like it's a definite 'ah-ha supernatural!' thing for there not to be a paradox. I suppose I'd say no to the spoof then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">A monster by any other name...</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1204-bridgewarden","name":"BridgeWarden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:56:40-07:00","id":129494,"title":"","content":"I'm not a mage player so I have to wonder. Going to play in a multi splat game so have to be sure I can keep up apperance of being just a skilled human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:46:44-07:00","id":129538,"title":"","content":"Unless it changes with the new chronicle book, or I'm mistaken, monsters of other types are treated the same as humans in terms of witnessing magic, so a demon is still subject to dis belief, and still causes paradox. Even if that's not the case, a mage doesn't really have a sense of when a witness will cause paradox or not. He can view the monster's aura (which the demon CAN spoof), but otherwise will have to make assumptions. Plus, paradox doesnt always occur. The mage might consider himself very lucky risking it around the monster, but won't assume no paradox must mean a supernatural observer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T21:24:26-07:00","id":129599,"title":"","content":"Ok, well good to know. I've never played mage only known hunters use paradox against mages (not always affected)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T23:31:50-07:00","id":129654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/129428-spoof-and-paradox?p=129538#post129538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it changes with the new chronicle book, or I'm mistaken, monsters of other types are treated the same as humans in terms of witnessing magic, so a demon is still subject to dis belief, and still causes paradox. Even if that's not the case, a mage doesn't really have a sense of when a witness will cause paradox or not. He can view the monster's aura (which the demon CAN spoof), but otherwise will have to make assumptions. Plus, paradox doesnt always occur. The mage might consider himself very lucky risking it around the monster, but won't assume no paradox must mean a supernatural observer.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, that was the complete opposite; Greater Templates do not conjure Disbelief or augment the chance of Paradox. Neither would a Demon; but they can 1) fake disbelief - I would, if I'm impersonating an office worker and someone shots a fireball out of nowhere, and my main concern is my cover, I would play along. Wouldn't be metagaming (the magic wouldn't unravel, tho) 2) the mage could scrutinize him, then he can simply spoof as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T07:51:47-07:00","id":129890,"title":"","content":"Well typically paradox is dependent on the spell. You throw a fireball in Awakening and its Vulgar even if you are 100 miles from anybody else. Mortals just increase the dice pool.<br /> <br /> Remember that characters do not have access to their sheets. They don't know how many dice they are rolling. Maybe the Demon is a supernatural or maybe the mage is just rolling very well, the character would not know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/463-derendel","name":"Derendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T08:33:08-07:00","id":129911,"title":"","content":"Its open to debate if Hunters count as Sleepers for the purpose of Awakened magic, let alone Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T09:46:53-07:00","id":129936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/129428-spoof-and-paradox?p=129911#post129911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its open to debate if Hunters count as Sleepers for the purpose of Awakened magic, let alone Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have a supernatural ability (Lucifuge) no they don't. If they don't, or rely on equipment or magic items (TFV) they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:30:53-07:00","id":129976,"title":"","content":"So does the Cheiron Group count as having a supernatural ability if they have a Thaumatechnology implant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2925-melange_thief","name":"Melange_Thief","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T13:44:52-07:00","id":130129,"title":"","content":"I would say no, I doubt gouls are different enough to so implants are neither in my opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T14:06:35-07:00","id":130157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melange_Thief</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/129428-spoof-and-paradox?p=129976#post129976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does the Cheiron Group count as having a supernatural ability if they have a Thaumatechnology implant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T22:03:18-07:00","id":131590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melange_Thief</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/129428-spoof-and-paradox?p=129976#post129976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does the Cheiron Group count as having a supernatural ability if they have a Thaumatechnology implant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's only &quot;supernatural&quot; in that it's &quot;weird&quot;. Thaumatechnology is &quot;simply&quot; highly strange implants. Cut it out and they lose it. Supernatural abilities a la Lucifuge are changes of the mind/soul, and THAT is what resonates with the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T22:05:39-07:00","id":131607,"title":"","content":"To answer OP:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/129428-spoof-and-paradox#post129428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If demon I is the lone one witnessing a mage do magic since no risk of paradox reveals that the demon isn't human can a demon chose to spoof this event?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK: A Demon does not aggravate Paradox nor render a spell Improbable. Spoofing doesn't play into witnessing anything, but if that Mage then tries to scrutinize you, you can indeed Spoof your cover. It is then resolved by Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}